on 4 supplies explicit families attaining each of these three numbers. Therefore no other integer \\(k\\) is possible.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{For every }n\\ge 3\\text{ the admissible values of }k\\text{ are }k=n-3,\\;n-2,\\;n.}\n\\]"
